1
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:08,342
[narrator] Until that moment...

2
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:11,595
when the earth bore a creature.

3
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:15,390
They only need a man so strong.

4
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:17,017
So powerful.

5
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:19,353
So daring.

6
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:20,646
Unstoppable.

7
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:22,231
Unshakeable.

8
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:25,651
- [thwacks]
- [grunts]

9
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:27,236
They need...

10
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:29,988
Monsour Del Rosario.

11
00:00:30,072 --> 00:00:31,198
Whatever demon you are

12
00:00:32,241 --> 00:00:33,742
I'm ready for you!

13
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:36,620
[narrator] Tornado Jack!

14
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:40,624
Facing dangers in the mouth of Hell

15
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:42,960
in the name of all that is good.

16
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:45,546
- [gunshot]
- [grunts]

17
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:48,799
- [zaps]
- [explosion]

18
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:50,342
[grunts]

19
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:53,804
[echoes] Tornado Jack!

20
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:04,690
[crew 1] Sir Monsour is late.

21
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:06,817
[crew 2] Yeah, I think
he's going to take longer.

22
00:01:08,694 --> 00:01:10,696
[crew 1] This might take a while.

23
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:12,322
- Let's eat first.
- Sorry, sir.

24
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:13,448
We're losing the sun.

25
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:15,409
Call him again.

26
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:19,871
[film rolling]

27
00:01:21,957 --> 00:01:23,959
[rolling continues]

28
00:01:24,835 --> 00:01:27,337
[thunder rumbles]

29
00:01:31,008 --> 00:01:33,385
[water pattering]

30
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:51,445
- [car approaches]
- [engine stops]

31
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:57,117
[Camille] Good morning.

32
00:01:57,868 --> 00:01:58,952
Good morning.

33
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:00,954
[Monsour grunts]

34
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,415
- [Monsour] Good morning.
- Good morning, Sir Monsour.

35
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:04,541
Good morning, Camille.

36
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:06,627
Uh... I saw the camera over there.

37
00:02:07,044 --> 00:02:10,047
Move it to the other side. Okay?

38
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:11,506
- Okay, sir.
- Okay?

39
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:13,342
- Is Lav there?
- Yes, he is.

40
00:02:13,425 --> 00:02:15,510
[explosion]

41
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:17,596
[heroic music]

42
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,683
- Good morning, Lav!
- [Lav] Hey!

43
00:02:22,017 --> 00:02:23,060
Is it still "morning"?

44
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:25,979
- [Monsour] Hey, let's talk.
- [Lav] Mm-hm.

45
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:28,940
Uh, I want to change
the camera position

46
00:02:29,024 --> 00:02:30,275
from the right to the left.

47
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:32,444
Because in all my films

48
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:35,656
my angle is always from the left,
never the right.

49
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:37,032
Secondly

50
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:39,159
I read the script.

51
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:42,621
I just left a scene
without saying a word.

52
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:45,791
I thought it would be good
if we put in some dialogues.

53
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:48,293
Let me know which one is better.

54
00:02:48,377 --> 00:02:50,629
This is version one.

55
00:02:51,171 --> 00:02:52,297
"Salazar...

56
00:02:53,674 --> 00:02:55,008
you'll pay for this!

57
00:02:55,092 --> 00:02:58,303
I'm taking this fight
all the way to hell!"

58
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:00,514
Ha? Now, this is version two.

59
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:02,432
[exhales]

60
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:06,144
"Salazar! We can do this in hell!

61
00:03:06,228 --> 00:03:07,854
You'll pay for this!"

62
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:09,523
[Monsour] What are we going with?

63
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:12,776
Version one or version two?

64
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:15,737
- The first one.
- Yeah!

65
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:17,906
That's what I thought!
I also really liked the first one.

66
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:21,910
Okay.
Caloy, I need to internalize now.

67
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:23,078
There they are!

68
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,204
See this, buddy?

69
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:25,914
This will do it.

70
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,750
Two, three.

71
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:31,378
And then right, here.

72
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:34,673
Me and my muscles will look
really angry in this movie!

73
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:36,591
I'll be over here. Okay.

74
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:38,719
Let's take it here, guys.

75
00:03:38,802 --> 00:03:40,053
Where's that girl from Shine?

76
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,346
Here, sir.

77
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:45,726
I need to speak to Andrea.
Where is she?

78
00:03:45,809 --> 00:03:48,353
She's at the office, I'll call her.

79
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:49,855
Yes!

80
00:03:51,732 --> 00:03:52,733
[grunts]

81
00:03:55,152 --> 00:03:56,278
Yes!

82
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:59,239
[tense music]

83
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:13,253
[Rina in English] Hey.

84
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:18,341
[in Filipino] Whatever happened
to waking up early

85
00:04:18,425 --> 00:04:21,511
and going home for fresh clothes?

86
00:04:22,053 --> 00:04:23,638
Sleeping in is way better.

87
00:04:23,722 --> 00:04:25,265
[chuckles]

88
00:04:29,603 --> 00:04:31,688
Why don't you go straight to work?

89
00:04:31,772 --> 00:04:33,106
[in English] Why do you
have to go home?

90
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:37,402
[in Filipino] The staff will see me
wearing yesterday's clothes.

91
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:40,030
[Joey] Am I going with you
to your office?

92
00:04:40,489 --> 00:04:42,824
Nope. Mommy's waiting for you.

93
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:48,079
Uh...

94
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:49,998
It's almost time to leave for Canada.

95
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:53,293
You have to start helping her pack.

96
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:55,754
Oh? Is this all you're taking?

97
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:58,340
- Can I zip this up?
- Wait! My robots!

98
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,802
[tense music]

99
00:05:17,776 --> 00:05:19,778
[tense music continues]

100
00:05:24,908 --> 00:05:26,326
- Next time...
- [Rina] Mm?

101
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:28,745
...pack a bag and leave it here.

102
00:05:28,829 --> 00:05:30,914
So you won't have to rush going home.

103
00:05:31,623 --> 00:05:32,749
That's a lot!

104
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:33,834
Of course!

105
00:05:33,917 --> 00:05:35,001
There's food at the office.

106
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:36,461
Do I have to bring all of these?

107
00:05:36,545 --> 00:05:39,005
You hardly eat, so yes, take it all.

108
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:41,383
Oh! Are you coming with me?

109
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:42,884
Yes, Andrea. I'm meeting some friends

110
00:05:42,968 --> 00:05:44,511
near your office before I go back

111
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:45,929
- to the apartment.
- Okay.

112
00:05:47,973 --> 00:05:48,974
Those two?

113
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:51,059
- Of course!
- Okay, put it here.

114
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:55,272
Here. This guy first.

115
00:05:55,355 --> 00:05:56,398
You have a lot of toys.

116
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:59,150
Make sure to pick up after yourself.

117
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:02,779
Your mom's going to be busy
with her work, okay?

118
00:06:03,572 --> 00:06:04,906
You should really come with us.

119
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:07,242
[Joey] You can pick up
my toys for me.

120
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:09,661
Tell Mommy to get you a ticket.

121
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:11,997
I think it's time to go. Come on!

122
00:06:13,957 --> 00:06:16,084
- Just lock the doors when you leave.
- Yes. Go.

123
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:18,378
- [Karylle] Bye!
- You're going to be late.

124
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:19,796
- [Andrea] Thank you!
- [Rina] Take care!

125
00:07:09,304 --> 00:07:11,514
[electricity crackles]

126
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:18,188
[smoke detector beeping]

127
00:07:24,319 --> 00:07:26,321
[theme music]

128
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:30,450
♪ Careful, careful ♪

129
00:07:31,493 --> 00:07:34,079
♪ The world is full
Of jealous people ♪

130
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:37,415
♪ When envy strikes,
It means trouble ♪

131
00:07:37,499 --> 00:07:39,834
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

132
00:07:39,918 --> 00:07:41,962
♪ Careful, careful ♪

133
00:07:43,046 --> 00:07:45,590
♪ We always need to be careful ♪

134
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:49,094
♪ Prying eyes ready to snoop ♪

135
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:52,305
♪ Digging for the juiciest scoop ♪

136
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:54,683
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

137
00:07:57,936 --> 00:08:00,397
♪ Careful, careful ♪

138
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:05,986
[suspenseful music]

139
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:12,325
SEN. FRANK TO ABS-CBN:
YOUR DAYS ARE NUMBERED!

140
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:19,708
Does ABS-CBN deserve to be shut down?

141
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:23,962
Frank Villacin is very influential.

142
00:08:24,045 --> 00:08:26,214
Frank Villacin is all bark.

143
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:28,758
- Mm-hm.
- [telephone ringing]

144
00:08:31,094 --> 00:08:32,429
[imitates Sofie]
Shine Artist Management.

145
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:34,472
This is Sofie. How may I help you?

146
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,809
[imitates Sofie]
Hello, yes. Sorry about that.

147
00:08:38,143 --> 00:08:40,812
[Noemi] Sure, I'll transfer you,
please hold.

148
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:43,773
- [Chin] Your impression was spot on!
- Where's Sofie?

149
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:45,483
And why is it so hot in here?

150
00:08:45,567 --> 00:08:46,818
- It's the AC.
- It's not working.

151
00:08:46,901 --> 00:08:48,194
Her audition is today.

152
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:49,320
Did you leave the set?

153
00:08:49,404 --> 00:08:51,448
- [Chin] You left?
- I said I had a meeting.

154
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:52,991
And I need a change of clothes.

155
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,784
Looks like we're going
into overtime again.

156
00:08:54,868 --> 00:08:55,910
A lot of problems on this set!

157
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:57,162
Hey, the meeting's about to start.

158
00:08:57,245 --> 00:08:58,872
I didn't know Sir Monsour was a diva.

159
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:00,582
[Camille] I was on the set
before he was.

160
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:01,833
- Can I leave this here?
- Sure.

161
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:02,917
[Noemi] What do you expect?

162
00:09:03,001 --> 00:09:05,253
It's been so long
since his last film.

163
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:06,796
- [Chin] That's right.
- [telephone rings]

164
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:07,964
- You guys go ahead.
- Okay.

165
00:09:08,506 --> 00:09:09,841
[Chin] Sir Samuel told stories
about him.

166
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:11,009
Hello?

167
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:12,510
[scoffs] Really?

168
00:09:12,594 --> 00:09:13,678
Wrong number.

169
00:09:13,762 --> 00:09:15,555
[playful music]

170
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:17,849
Why do you think
he's making a comeback?

171
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:19,142
Do you think he needs money?

172
00:09:19,225 --> 00:09:20,602
No, he doesn't.

173
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:22,896
He's producing this film, right?

174
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:25,398
No wonder he acts like
he's king of the set.

175
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:28,359
I heard he's always been like that.

176
00:09:35,033 --> 00:09:36,576
[Chin] It's so hot!

177
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:39,079
[Noemi] Deo, what is this?

178
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:40,955
What's going on?

179
00:09:41,915 --> 00:09:42,999
[Chin] It's really hot!

180
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:45,960
Matthew, weren't you wearing that
the other day?

181
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:48,630
[Matthew] What?

182
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,298
What you have on.

183
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:51,382
[Andrea] You were wearing that

184
00:09:51,466 --> 00:09:52,759
- the other day.
- [Matthew] I like it.

185
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:03,895
Okay, so for the next two years,
Rob is fully booked.

186
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:07,941
And the tax people have agreed
that the ads he'll do for them

187
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:09,359
will cover for his unpaid taxes.

188
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:12,070
Problem solved.
His projects will proceed as planned.

189
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:13,446
[in English] Okay. Great job!

190
00:10:13,822 --> 00:10:15,198
Um...

191
00:10:15,281 --> 00:10:16,324
Is there anything else?

192
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:17,450
Yes!

193
00:10:18,576 --> 00:10:20,912
[in Filipino] Shouldn't we tell them?
Let's tell them the good news!

194
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,080
What good news?

195
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:23,206
[Andrea] About SAM!

196
00:10:23,289 --> 00:10:24,374
[Matthew] Andrea.

197
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:27,293
I don't think we should.
We're not sure yet.

198
00:10:27,377 --> 00:10:30,213
This is our core group.
They have to know, and...

199
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:31,756
Okay, anyway.

200
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:35,426
Guys, Matthew, Gabriel, and I

201
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:37,095
will be buying SAM

202
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:38,930
from Mrs. Helen Mendiola!

203
00:10:39,013 --> 00:10:41,349
Oh, my god! Thank you, Lord!

204
00:10:41,432 --> 00:10:42,976
I thought I was losing this job!

205
00:10:43,226 --> 00:10:45,186
So you're each paying one-third?

206
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:48,273
Well, Matthew and Gina

207
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:49,649
will pay for half.

208
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:50,859
[Andrea] And Gabriel and I will...

209
00:10:50,942 --> 00:10:53,611
No, I don't think
we need to go into detail.

210
00:10:53,695 --> 00:10:55,822
[chuckles] Well, whatever.

211
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:58,616
- Anyway, SAM will be ours.
- [Chin] Love it.

212
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:01,035
[Gab] But for sure,
we'll need your help.

213
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:04,164
We need as many talents as we can get
to join SAM.

214
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:09,502
And maybe now is the best time
to start our Social Media division.

215
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:12,338
- Agree!
- For sure! I have so many ideas.

216
00:11:12,422 --> 00:11:14,924
Of course, we won't be able
to handle all that

217
00:11:15,008 --> 00:11:16,259
on top of everything else.

218
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:18,511
So Gab and I were thinking

219
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:22,098
of choosing one person
to head that division.

220
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:25,059
So Chin and I go head-to-head?

221
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:26,644
Camille too!

222
00:11:27,562 --> 00:11:30,648
[Andrea] I know she's new,
but she's doing such a great job.

223
00:11:30,732 --> 00:11:33,318
Who knows? She could make
a great Junior Manager.

224
00:11:34,152 --> 00:11:35,737
- You all have an equal chance.
- Mm-hm.

225
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,322
- Yeah.
- So, good luck, guys!

226
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:40,200
[Daisy] Ladies and gentlemen!

227
00:11:40,283 --> 00:11:42,619
How about some arroz caldo?

228
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:44,662
- [Gab] Arroz caldo?
- [Andrea] In this heat?

229
00:11:44,746 --> 00:11:45,955
- I have packed lunch.
- Ms. Andrea.

230
00:11:46,039 --> 00:11:47,373
- Yes?
- I'll head back to set

231
00:11:47,457 --> 00:11:49,751
after I go home
for a change of clothes.

232
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,628
Sir Monsour lent his car and driver.

233
00:11:51,711 --> 00:11:53,630
- Okay. How is Lav?
- Oh, Mr. Lav says

234
00:11:53,713 --> 00:11:55,882
- he needs to speak to you urgently.
- Okay, please set it up.

235
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,050
- Let me know. Thank you.
- Okay.

236
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:59,219
- How about some steamed rice cake?
- I'll go get my lunch.

237
00:11:59,302 --> 00:12:00,970
- [Gab] Let me have some of it.
- This'll do.

238
00:12:01,054 --> 00:12:03,556
[Andrea] Come with me.
I don't want to have to return.

239
00:12:05,892 --> 00:12:07,852
- [Gab] Put this on my tab, okay?
- [Daisy] Yes, Gab!

240
00:12:07,936 --> 00:12:10,355
I've never been this nervous before.

241
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:12,607
I've auditioned many times before

242
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:13,775
but my heart was going so fast.

243
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:15,652
That's how it goes, get used to it.

244
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:17,737
What did they say?

245
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:20,406
I'm not sure, I couldn't read them.

246
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:22,659
Sir Gab, did they call yet?

247
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:24,827
You just got back! Relax.

248
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:26,955
Oh, by the way.

249
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:29,165
- Where's Joey? Thanks, bro!
- Hey, congrats!

250
00:12:29,249 --> 00:12:30,959
[Sofie] I got him
a going-away present.

251
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:32,585
- Really?
- Mm-hm.

252
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:35,046
[Gab] He already went back to Lora's.
They have to start packing.

253
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:37,131
They're leaving soon.

254
00:12:37,215 --> 00:12:39,550
- They're really going to Canada?
- [Gab] Yes.

255
00:12:39,634 --> 00:12:40,927
[Sofie] No going-away party?

256
00:12:41,469 --> 00:12:42,762
- A going-away party?
- [Sofie] Yeah.

257
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:44,264
For a six-year-old?

258
00:12:44,347 --> 00:12:46,641
- Yeah!
- [Andrea] Why not? It'll be fun.

259
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:47,892
[Sofie] Right! Where do we have it?

260
00:12:47,976 --> 00:12:49,143
Your place, Sir Gab?

261
00:12:49,227 --> 00:12:51,229
No, his place is too small.

262
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:52,438
We'll do it here.

263
00:12:52,814 --> 00:12:53,982
Hey, that's harsh.

264
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:56,025
But the AC's not working.

265
00:12:56,109 --> 00:12:59,070
Then let's rent
some huge electric fans.

266
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:01,823
And Rina will take care of the food.

267
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:04,492
[gasps] Ma'am, I want in!

268
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:06,035
- [Andrea] Of course.
- Here's what we'll do.

269
00:13:06,119 --> 00:13:07,328
I'll take care of everything.

270
00:13:07,412 --> 00:13:08,913
Just tell Ms. Lora

271
00:13:08,997 --> 00:13:10,498
to invite all of Joey's friends.

272
00:13:10,581 --> 00:13:12,250
And let's invite Mother Aleta.

273
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:14,210
I want to see her in costume!

274
00:13:14,294 --> 00:13:16,671
[Andrea] Oh, yeah, a costume party!

275
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:17,964
- Costume?
- This will be great!

276
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:20,049
- Costume?
- Everyone get your costumes ready.

277
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:22,218
- Costumes?
- For Joey's going-away party.

278
00:13:22,302 --> 00:13:23,594
- Game? Game!
- [Sofie] Let's go!

279
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:25,847
- [all cheering]
- Game!

280
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:28,308
[dramatic music]

281
00:13:46,284 --> 00:13:48,161
[wind chimes clink]

282
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:50,580
[Camille] That's what Mama said.

283
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:52,248
It was the Ad Congress.

284
00:13:52,332 --> 00:13:53,333
He walked in...

285
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:54,459
You mean Pops.

286
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:59,005
Sir Matthew and Sir Paul walked in,
and they wanted haircuts.

287
00:14:00,131 --> 00:14:03,134
They couldn't find a barber.

288
00:14:03,217 --> 00:14:04,469
So they walked into Mama's salon.

289
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:08,264
That was it.

290
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:10,141
- From then on...
- From then on

291
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,726
he would go up to Baguio regularly.

292
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:14,062
Pops admitted that.

293
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:16,230
Mama doesn't remember.

294
00:14:16,314 --> 00:14:17,815
Or maybe she just didn't notice.

295
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:20,777
Why did they break up?

296
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:24,072
[exhales sharply]
Maybe they got tired of it all.

297
00:14:24,906 --> 00:14:26,282
I never asked Mama.

298
00:14:27,492 --> 00:14:29,327
[Camille] But believe me,
we don't know you.

299
00:14:30,078 --> 00:14:33,122
I mean, we know nothing about you.

300
00:14:33,998 --> 00:14:36,167
All I know was that
Matthew had another family...

301
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,460
Yes, you are.

302
00:14:38,211 --> 00:14:39,462
The other family that jerk had...

303
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:40,671
[shouts] Don't be mad at him!

304
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,716
[bed creaks]

305
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:47,929
[softly] Don't be mad.

306
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:50,098
It's not his fault.

307
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:51,516
I came to see him.

308
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:55,228
I wanted to work with him.

309
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:56,687
I wanted to be with him.

310
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:58,815
I'm not mad at him.

311
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,442
Besides, we always fight.

312
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:02,693
This is nothing new.

313
00:15:04,654 --> 00:15:05,988
If you're not mad at him...

314
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:09,117
are you mad at me?

315
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:12,829
No.

316
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:14,872
Maybe a little, I don't know.

317
00:15:16,541 --> 00:15:18,459
I don't like
seeing my mother this way.

318
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:20,753
She's always crying.

319
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,881
I don't know how to make her stop.

320
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:29,220
You're lucky.

321
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:31,931
You get to spend every day with him.

322
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:34,725
That's what you want, right?

323
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:41,232
What do you call him?

324
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:43,734
"Sir Matthew."

325
00:15:44,569 --> 00:15:45,570
"Matthew."

326
00:15:45,987 --> 00:15:47,029
Shoot.

327
00:15:48,114 --> 00:15:50,199
So nobody knows? Not even one?

328
00:15:56,414 --> 00:15:58,082
[Hector] You're going back
to the shoot?

329
00:15:58,166 --> 00:15:59,917
Yeah, I hate my life.

330
00:16:00,001 --> 00:16:01,252
- Why? [gasps]
- Ouch.

331
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:02,336
- Did you miss a step?
- Sorry.

332
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,797
Told you I'm exhausted. Sorry.

333
00:16:04,881 --> 00:16:06,215
- Oh, god!
- What?

334
00:16:06,299 --> 00:16:08,092
This is where I dropped you off
after our date.

335
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:09,802
Yeah, so?

336
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:15,224
- [gasps]
- Let's not talk about it.

337
00:16:15,308 --> 00:16:16,434
- This is the last time.
- I know.

338
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:17,560
[Camille] You started it.

339
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:18,728
- Never again.
- Nothing happened.

340
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:21,063
- No. Nothing happened. Okay.
- Okay.

341
00:16:21,147 --> 00:16:22,356
Yuck, bro.

342
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,649
You mean, "Big Bro".

343
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:24,817
Yes, Big Bro is right.

344
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:25,902
Right.

345
00:16:27,028 --> 00:16:28,988
- Oh, the car's here.
- That's Monsour Del Rosario's car?

346
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:30,156
Yes, I borrowed it.

347
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:32,116
Gotta run, I'm going to be late.

348
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:36,329
- Call me!
- [Hector] Call me anytime.

349
00:16:39,665 --> 00:16:41,834
[mouse clicks]

350
00:16:41,918 --> 00:16:43,211
Sir Matthew?

351
00:16:46,339 --> 00:16:49,008
What a big opportunity

352
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:51,052
this Junior Manager position is!

353
00:16:51,761 --> 00:16:52,762
[Matthew mumbles]

354
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:56,474
- [Matthew] Oh...
- That's what I really want to do.

355
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:59,101
[Noemi] To manage talents
just like you do.

356
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:00,228
[in English] I mean...

357
00:17:00,311 --> 00:17:01,729
You are my inspiration.

358
00:17:02,355 --> 00:17:04,649
- I consider you my mentor.
- [high-pitched ringing]

359
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:06,526
[Matthew] Gina,
I came here to apologize.

360
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:08,653
It was a long time ago.

361
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:10,363
You would've never found out.

362
00:17:10,905 --> 00:17:13,157
That is, if you didn't hire her
to work for you.

363
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,408
That bastard child of yours.

364
00:17:14,492 --> 00:17:15,535
I didn't hire her.

365
00:17:16,953 --> 00:17:18,329
She works for Andrea.

366
00:17:18,955 --> 00:17:21,082
Do you know what you've done
to those children?

367
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:25,753
[Gina] I suppose you're here

368
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:27,129
for your check.

369
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:30,508
The money you're going to buy
your plaything with?

370
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:32,218
The money to pay for Shine?

371
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:38,766
[Gina] Why don't you just go ahead
and move to Galaxy?

372
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:40,101
That should solve all your problems.

373
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:41,435
[Noemi] Sir Matthew?

374
00:17:42,228 --> 00:17:43,271
Sir Matthew?

375
00:17:44,689 --> 00:17:45,731
Oh, I'm sorry.

376
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:47,608
Uh... What were you saying?

377
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:51,112
Is there anything you need me to do?

378
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:53,739
You know, so you can evaluate
my performance.

379
00:17:57,910 --> 00:17:59,412
Nothing at the moment.

380
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,750
Oh, no, hang on, there is something.

381
00:18:04,834 --> 00:18:06,085
Yes, Sir Matthew? Let me know.

382
00:18:06,168 --> 00:18:08,296
- What is it, I'll take care of it.
- Here. Wait.

383
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:10,423
Can you get me three new shirts?

384
00:18:10,798 --> 00:18:11,924
Just like this one.

385
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:14,552
But maybe other colors.
I'm sure you know my size.

386
00:18:15,803 --> 00:18:16,804
Mm-hm.

387
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:19,682
- Hi.
- [Andrea] Oh!

388
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:20,766
[chuckles]

389
00:18:22,393 --> 00:18:23,728
Ms. Gutierrez.

390
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,229
So good to see you again.

391
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:28,566
Why do you always give me
a hard time, Andrea?

392
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:30,484
- What?
- [Janine] Oh, please.

393
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:32,445
I know what you're doing, Andrea.

394
00:18:33,112 --> 00:18:34,947
I was already in talks with HBO!

395
00:18:35,031 --> 00:18:38,326
I want that part in Rob's film.

396
00:18:38,868 --> 00:18:40,494
Why are you blocking this for me?

397
00:18:41,287 --> 00:18:43,539
Janine, we've done no such thing.

398
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:47,376
As a team, we decided
that it is in our best interest

399
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:51,422
to have Rob supported
by an all-SAM cast.

400
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:53,215
And HBO agreed.

401
00:18:53,299 --> 00:18:54,342
I'm surprised

402
00:18:55,051 --> 00:18:56,677
your manager failed to inform you.

403
00:18:57,887 --> 00:19:00,139
I haven't signed with Galaxy yet.

404
00:19:00,890 --> 00:19:03,934
[Andrea] Well,
whether you sign or not

405
00:19:04,018 --> 00:19:06,354
bottom line is,
if you're not a SAM artist

406
00:19:06,437 --> 00:19:08,064
you can't be part of the project.

407
00:19:08,731 --> 00:19:11,442
[frustrated sigh] So what do I do?

408
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:13,527
[in English] I want that part.

409
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:16,822
Then come back to SAM.

410
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:19,116
[scoffs]

411
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:23,412
[sighs]
I knew you were going to say that.

412
00:19:23,496 --> 00:19:24,914
SAM is your home.

413
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:26,916
You belong with us.

414
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:29,460
This is a long-standing relationship.

415
00:19:29,919 --> 00:19:31,128
And I agree with you.

416
00:19:31,212 --> 00:19:32,963
You're perfect for this project.

417
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:36,258
But again,
you cannot be part of this project

418
00:19:36,342 --> 00:19:38,260
if you are not a SAM artist.

419
00:19:39,345 --> 00:19:41,222
And this thing you say I do?

420
00:19:41,305 --> 00:19:42,431
I would do it for you.

421
00:19:43,849 --> 00:19:44,934
I always do.

422
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:49,522
I don't want to audition.

423
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:52,066
I can have that arranged.

424
00:19:53,484 --> 00:19:55,444
Just send me the contract.

425
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:01,575
I'm a good actor, Andrea.

426
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:03,327
I know.

427
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:07,623
But, Janine,
it's not always about talent.

428
00:20:13,796 --> 00:20:15,798
[tense music]

429
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:17,925
WHAT'S THE TEA?
WITH OGIE DIAZ

430
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:19,385
Shh! Be quiet.

431
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:20,469
Be quiet.

432
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:21,929
They might find out

433
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:24,765
that we know all about their secret!

434
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:26,392
Who am I talking about?

435
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:28,185
The Power Couple

436
00:20:28,269 --> 00:20:32,148
who's having marital issues.

437
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:34,233
That's tough!

438
00:20:34,316 --> 00:20:36,569
From Sports Power Couple

439
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,988
to Power Outage.

440
00:20:39,071 --> 00:20:42,074
[gasps]
The relationship is blacking out.

441
00:20:42,158 --> 00:20:44,994
But what about their endorsements?

442
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:47,121
That's their livelihood.

443
00:20:47,204 --> 00:20:48,998
I heard these two would often

444
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:51,792
go out in public

445
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:53,919
to show people that they're together.

446
00:20:54,003 --> 00:20:55,087
That it's all good between them.

447
00:20:55,171 --> 00:20:58,382
But behind the scenes, gosh...

448
00:20:58,466 --> 00:21:01,427
The truth is, they have issues.

449
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:04,764
But please don't judge them.

450
00:21:04,847 --> 00:21:08,225
You think they're putting on an act?

451
00:21:08,309 --> 00:21:10,519
Oh, of course they'll do that.

452
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:11,896
It's just business.

453
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:14,440
Try to empathize with them.

454
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:17,151
But hold on. Here it is!

455
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:18,527
Let me give you a clue.

456
00:21:18,611 --> 00:21:19,987
All you bashers out there...

457
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:21,447
POW!

458
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:22,698
...will get a taste of my fist!

459
00:21:22,782 --> 00:21:24,742
Ouch!

460
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,202
[squeals]

461
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:28,162
WHAT'S THE TEA?
WITH OGIE DIAZ

462
00:21:28,245 --> 00:21:29,663
- [Lav] Sound!
- [crew 1] Rolling!

463
00:21:29,747 --> 00:21:30,748
[Lav] Camera!

464
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:34,335
- Action!
- [Monsour shouts, grunts]

465
00:21:38,714 --> 00:21:39,715
[Lav] Exit!

466
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:42,051
Cut!

467
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:47,139
Lester.

468
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:48,724
Lester.

469
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:53,187
- Show him. Demonstrate, just do it.
- Okay.

470
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:54,271
Monsour.

471
00:21:54,355 --> 00:21:56,232
Monsour. Buddy.

472
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:57,608
We'll show you how we want it, okay?

473
00:21:57,858 --> 00:21:59,276
- Just to nail the blocking.
- [Emir] Sir.

474
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:01,111
[Emir] JR, Lester, ready?

475
00:22:01,195 --> 00:22:02,947
- [Lester] Ready.
- [Emir] Action.

476
00:22:03,364 --> 00:22:04,949
[both grunt]

477
00:22:09,578 --> 00:22:10,788
[Lav] Get up then exit right away.

478
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:12,122
Do it that way, okay?

479
00:22:13,541 --> 00:22:14,834
Get the blowers ready! Come on.

480
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,168
Action!

481
00:22:16,961 --> 00:22:19,380
[grunts]

482
00:22:21,423 --> 00:22:22,424
[Lav] Action!

483
00:22:25,678 --> 00:22:26,720
Exit now!

484
00:22:28,430 --> 00:22:29,849
Cut! Emir!

485
00:22:30,349 --> 00:22:31,433
What is it, sir?

486
00:22:31,517 --> 00:22:33,561
He's doing it again!
Is there a rock there or something?

487
00:22:33,644 --> 00:22:34,728
- I'll check.
- Is his foot stuck?

488
00:22:37,982 --> 00:22:40,609
- [Emir] There's nothing here.
- [Lav] Okay, reset! Sound!

489
00:22:40,693 --> 00:22:41,986
Wait, where's the alien guy?

490
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:44,029
- Camera!
- [crew 2] Take 17!

491
00:22:44,113 --> 00:22:46,365
- [grunts]
- Cut!

492
00:22:46,448 --> 00:22:48,742
[action music]

493
00:22:48,826 --> 00:22:50,953
Wind, we need wind!
One more, one more!

494
00:22:51,036 --> 00:22:53,122
- [Lav] Camera!
- [crew 2] Take 40!

495
00:22:53,706 --> 00:22:54,707
Action!

496
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:55,791
Wait, is this the right spot?

497
00:22:55,875 --> 00:22:56,917
How's my profile?

498
00:22:57,001 --> 00:22:58,002
[Lav] Action!

499
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:00,671
[grunts]

500
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:05,301
Cut!

501
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:06,427
Cut!

502
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:07,511
Cut!

503
00:23:07,928 --> 00:23:09,013
Cut!

504
00:23:09,972 --> 00:23:11,015
Hey, buddy?

505
00:23:13,976 --> 00:23:15,144
How exactly do you run?

506
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:20,107
I don't do that.

507
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:21,692
I get in my car.

508
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:24,111
Okay, one more.

509
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:25,529
Let's finish this tomorrow, sir.

510
00:23:25,613 --> 00:23:26,655
I need to be somewhere.

511
00:23:27,156 --> 00:23:29,241
This is so easy.
I can do it with my eyes closed.

512
00:23:29,575 --> 00:23:31,535
Tomorrow, I'll nail it in one take.

513
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:33,120
Camille.

514
00:23:33,329 --> 00:23:34,371
[Camille] Sir?

515
00:23:34,455 --> 00:23:36,206
Please tell Andrea I need to see her.

516
00:23:36,290 --> 00:23:38,834
It's important that we talk soon.

517
00:23:38,918 --> 00:23:40,461
- Yes, sir.
- This is urgent. ASAP.

518
00:23:40,544 --> 00:23:41,670
- Okay.
- Tell her right away.

519
00:23:41,754 --> 00:23:44,256
Uh, sir, don't you want to finish...

520
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:45,382
No, I don't.

521
00:23:45,758 --> 00:23:46,842
I'll do it tomorrow.

522
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:47,927
That'll be easy.

523
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:50,346
- [Monsour] Bye.
- [Lav] Camille.

524
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:51,555
- Hey!
- [Emir] Camille.

525
00:23:51,639 --> 00:23:55,059
Remember, you asked for this.
You wanted Lav to direct this movie.

526
00:23:55,142 --> 00:23:59,313
What I really wanted was something
with an "international" vibe!

527
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:01,190
This is my comeback movie!

528
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:03,984
I thought you were ready
to go commercial?

529
00:24:04,068 --> 00:24:06,737
I gave you everything you asked for

530
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:07,947
and I know...

531
00:24:08,489 --> 00:24:10,199
no one watches action movies anymore.

532
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:11,867
But I agreed to do this project.

533
00:24:11,951 --> 00:24:15,079
There's a certain quality
that my fans look for.

534
00:24:15,162 --> 00:24:16,163
Those iconic

535
00:24:16,372 --> 00:24:19,291
Monsour freaking Del Rosario moves!

536
00:24:19,375 --> 00:24:20,542
Bam! Just like that!

537
00:24:20,626 --> 00:24:23,128
You asked me
to write a normal script.

538
00:24:23,212 --> 00:24:25,422
Where's the script?

539
00:24:25,506 --> 00:24:26,757
Here is my Norte script.

540
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:28,092
[Lav] Forty pages.

541
00:24:28,175 --> 00:24:29,718
This is Monsour's script.

542
00:24:29,802 --> 00:24:31,053
A hundred and thirty pages.

543
00:24:31,136 --> 00:24:32,554
The lines are so long!

544
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:34,390
Look at how fat that script is!

545
00:24:34,473 --> 00:24:39,812
And I do nothing in it,
but cry and moan and think.

546
00:24:39,895 --> 00:24:41,271
Where's the martial arts?

547
00:24:41,897 --> 00:24:43,857
I agreed to keep it
under three hours.

548
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:46,026
That's a big ask but you got it!

549
00:24:46,110 --> 00:24:47,444
We've shot several days.

550
00:24:47,695 --> 00:24:50,906
I've done nothing but walk!

551
00:24:51,532 --> 00:24:53,575
"Walk, Monsour, keep walking."

552
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:55,035
What kind of an actor is he?

553
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:56,954
What kind of director is he?

554
00:24:57,037 --> 00:24:58,205
Can we replace him?

555
00:24:58,288 --> 00:25:00,165
How? He's producing this!

556
00:25:00,249 --> 00:25:01,667
[Monsour] This is my money
we're using.

557
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:02,835
I'm the lead actor.

558
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:04,211
But where's my face?

559
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:05,796
All you see are trees!

560
00:25:05,879 --> 00:25:07,214
None of it is authentic.

561
00:25:07,297 --> 00:25:09,508
"Monsour, you're overacting."

562
00:25:09,591 --> 00:25:11,427
So what? A movie isn't real life.

563
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:12,678
Sir, there's one more thing.

564
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:13,971
What now?

565
00:25:14,054 --> 00:25:15,514
I hate black and white!

566
00:25:15,597 --> 00:25:16,724
Did he say why?

567
00:25:16,807 --> 00:25:18,183
You can't see the blood!

568
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:19,893
An action movie in black and white!

569
00:25:19,977 --> 00:25:21,186
You can't tell if it's blood or oil!

570
00:25:21,270 --> 00:25:22,896
Darn, what the heck!

571
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:24,273
[chuckles] Goodness.

572
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:26,275
[in English]
It's all black and white!

573
00:25:27,776 --> 00:25:29,987
The world is black and white!

574
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:32,281
[in Ilonggo]
You better stop him or else!

575
00:25:32,364 --> 00:25:33,574
[in English] Color is an illusion!

576
00:25:33,657 --> 00:25:35,784
[in Ilonggo] I hate working with him!
Find a way!

577
00:25:35,868 --> 00:25:37,202
- [in English] Okay.
- Sorry.

578
00:25:37,286 --> 00:25:39,288
[in Filipino] I'm calm now,
but I really need a drink.

579
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:40,581
Oh, Camille!

580
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:42,499
[in Ilonggo]
Get the fan here before I explode!

581
00:25:42,583 --> 00:25:43,792
[in English] Old Fashioned? Bourbon?

582
00:25:43,876 --> 00:25:45,252
- What do you want?
- Marijuana.

583
00:25:45,335 --> 00:25:46,336
Marijuana?

584
00:25:46,420 --> 00:25:48,172
[in Filipino]
We have that. Check in my office.

585
00:25:48,255 --> 00:25:50,674
[in Ilonggo] Award-winning
international filmmaker, whatever!

586
00:25:52,551 --> 00:25:54,386
[in English]
Please, Andrea, I'm begging you.

587
00:25:55,804 --> 00:25:57,306
Can you fix this for me?

588
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:01,143
Of course!

589
00:26:01,727 --> 00:26:04,021
[in Filipino] Don't worry, Lav.
I'll talk to the investors.

590
00:26:04,104 --> 00:26:05,606
I'm sure we can figure something out.

591
00:26:05,689 --> 00:26:06,774
[in English] Just give me time.

592
00:26:06,857 --> 00:26:08,817
[in Filipino] Okay.
Make sure we can see the blood.

593
00:26:08,901 --> 00:26:10,736
Convince them, Andrea.

594
00:26:10,819 --> 00:26:11,862
Oh, of course!

595
00:26:11,945 --> 00:26:14,364
Of course! The blood!
We'll know it's blood.

596
00:26:14,448 --> 00:26:15,574
Oh, by the way.

597
00:26:15,657 --> 00:26:17,201
We're having a party here.

598
00:26:17,284 --> 00:26:19,369
- Please come.
- A costume party?

599
00:26:19,453 --> 00:26:21,955
- I'll come if he won't.
- Monsour?

600
00:26:22,039 --> 00:26:23,665
- Lav can't be here.
- Oh!

601
00:26:23,749 --> 00:26:24,792
I'll make sure of that.

602
00:26:24,875 --> 00:26:26,210
He won't be here.

603
00:26:26,293 --> 00:26:28,003
- I'll make sure of that.
- [Lav] Okay, make sure.

604
00:26:28,087 --> 00:26:29,755
- [Monsour] Okay, bye!
- Bye!

605
00:26:34,093 --> 00:26:37,554
[Camille] Thank god for the fridge.

606
00:26:37,638 --> 00:26:39,014
Whose fault is it?

607
00:26:39,098 --> 00:26:41,183
They both have a point.

608
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:42,309
My god.

609
00:26:42,392 --> 00:26:44,770
SAM can't lose this project.

610
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:46,355
Camille, we just can't!

611
00:26:46,438 --> 00:26:48,482
[gasps] What's up?

612
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:50,442
Wanna join us, Ms. Daisy?

613
00:26:51,151 --> 00:26:52,319
[Daisy] You want what I'm selling?

614
00:26:52,402 --> 00:26:54,738
[Andrea] Sorry,
can't eat in this heat, Daisy.

615
00:26:56,406 --> 00:26:57,616
[groans]

616
00:26:57,699 --> 00:26:58,992
What heat?

617
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:00,369
[Daisy] What heat?

618
00:27:00,452 --> 00:27:01,995
- [gasps]
- Does it come with batteries?

619
00:27:02,079 --> 00:27:03,288
Of course!

620
00:27:03,372 --> 00:27:04,748
- It's automatic!
- [Andrea] What is that?

621
00:27:04,832 --> 00:27:06,667
- [Camille] Ms. Andrea...
- Ready to use!

622
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:09,962
And if you run out of batteries,
don't worry, because...

623
00:27:10,838 --> 00:27:13,090
- These run on manual power!
- [Camille] Nice!

624
00:27:13,173 --> 00:27:14,508
Go get my purse, now!

625
00:27:14,591 --> 00:27:16,844
- No need. I have cash.
- You do?

626
00:27:16,927 --> 00:27:18,887
- [Daisy] I can put it on your tab.
- Here.

627
00:27:18,971 --> 00:27:20,055
But cash is good too!

628
00:27:20,139 --> 00:27:21,306
What does this one do?

629
00:27:21,390 --> 00:27:22,391
Madam.

630
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:24,351
This is what celebrities use on set.

631
00:27:24,434 --> 00:27:25,561
Try it on.

632
00:27:25,644 --> 00:27:27,062
- Ouch!
- I'm sorry.

633
00:27:27,146 --> 00:27:28,856
- Can I use these at once?
- Like this.

634
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:36,530
[Sofie] This way, please.

635
00:27:40,868 --> 00:27:41,994
[knocks on door]

636
00:27:42,077 --> 00:27:43,620
Sir Matthew, he needs your signature.

637
00:27:43,704 --> 00:27:44,705
[Matthew] Okay.

638
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:48,292
- [mailman] Thank you, sir.
- [Matthew] Thank you.

639
00:27:49,543 --> 00:27:51,712
[tense music]

640
00:27:51,795 --> 00:27:53,005
[Paul] Helen is livid!

641
00:27:53,714 --> 00:27:57,134
She was ready to accept my offer
to buy Shine.

642
00:27:57,426 --> 00:27:59,011
And now I'm withdrawing the offer.

643
00:27:59,094 --> 00:28:00,220
[Matthew] Well...

644
00:28:00,304 --> 00:28:02,723
Paul, what did you just send me?

645
00:28:05,309 --> 00:28:06,810
[Paul] There's just one other offer

646
00:28:06,894 --> 00:28:11,231
but I'm pretty sure Helen
isn't taking that offer.

647
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:15,777
That way, Andrea and Gabriel
can buy Shine.

648
00:28:15,861 --> 00:28:17,821
And then you can move to us.

649
00:28:18,906 --> 00:28:22,868
What you have in your hand
is your signing bonus.

650
00:28:22,951 --> 00:28:23,994
And Matthew?

651
00:28:25,078 --> 00:28:26,830
I'm so excited.

652
00:28:27,122 --> 00:28:30,709
Okay, well, let me study it first.

653
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:32,002
I'll get back to you.

654
00:28:37,716 --> 00:28:38,759
Yes, Camille?

655
00:28:39,509 --> 00:28:40,761
Here, for the heat.

656
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:42,221
The others have theirs already.

657
00:28:42,971 --> 00:28:44,389
- [Matthew] Thank you.
- Try it.

658
00:28:44,473 --> 00:28:45,515
Make sure it works.

659
00:28:51,355 --> 00:28:53,315
- [wind blows]
- Wow, it's strong!

660
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:54,608
- Let me get that.
- No, I'll do it.

661
00:28:54,691 --> 00:28:56,235
- I'll do it.
- [Camille] It's okay, I have it.

662
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:04,618
Yes?

663
00:29:04,993 --> 00:29:06,328
I just wanted to give you that.

664
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:07,496
Thank you.

665
00:29:12,292 --> 00:29:13,335
Matthew.

666
00:29:14,002 --> 00:29:15,754
I had a talk with Hector.

667
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:24,930
[in English]
Yes! I'm available on that day.

668
00:29:25,013 --> 00:29:26,056
[Kelly] That's great, Gabriel!

669
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:28,100
That's the only time we could see you

670
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:32,604
otherwise we'd be waiting for a month
and we just can't wait that long.

671
00:29:32,688 --> 00:29:35,857
[Gab] We're very excited to finalize
Kiray's contract for Women in Chains.

672
00:29:35,941 --> 00:29:38,193
Great, we'll see you then.

673
00:29:38,277 --> 00:29:39,611
Great! All right! See you!

674
00:29:40,153 --> 00:29:41,154
[in Filipino] Sir Gab?

675
00:29:41,238 --> 00:29:45,033
The meeting with Kelly Norman
is on Joey and Lora's departure.

676
00:29:45,450 --> 00:29:47,327
- Oh, really?
- [Chin] Yes.

677
00:29:47,411 --> 00:29:49,997
It should be a quick meeting.
I'll make it to the airport in time.

678
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:51,290
I hope you're sure about that.

679
00:29:51,665 --> 00:29:52,874
- Here.
- [Gab] What's this?

680
00:29:52,958 --> 00:29:55,168
- This heat is killing us.
- [Gab] Right.

681
00:29:55,252 --> 00:29:57,254
[cell phone ringing]

682
00:29:58,005 --> 00:29:59,047
[in English] Hello?

683
00:29:59,131 --> 00:30:00,757
Yes, this is Gabriel Soler.

684
00:30:01,967 --> 00:30:03,010
Sofie Lasola?

685
00:30:03,677 --> 00:30:04,970
[in Filipino] Yes, absolutely!

686
00:30:06,388 --> 00:30:07,889
[Gab] I'm looking at it right now.

687
00:30:07,973 --> 00:30:10,350
Sorry, she's been on demand lately.

688
00:30:10,434 --> 00:30:11,560
[in English] Okay, which role?

689
00:30:13,312 --> 00:30:14,563
Okay, what page?

690
00:30:16,106 --> 00:30:17,107
[Sofie] Okay.

691
00:30:17,190 --> 00:30:19,443
- Thank you so much. Thank you.
- [Gab clears throat]

692
00:30:19,526 --> 00:30:20,861
- [Chin] Sofie?
- Yes?

693
00:30:20,944 --> 00:30:23,030
[in Filipino]
Sir Gab has something to tell you.

694
00:30:23,363 --> 00:30:24,406
Uh...

695
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:25,699
You said you'll do it.

696
00:30:25,782 --> 00:30:28,327
Uh, Sofie, about your audition.

697
00:30:29,911 --> 00:30:30,954
Did I get it?

698
00:30:33,707 --> 00:30:34,750
Yes, but

699
00:30:35,208 --> 00:30:37,502
you're the secretary
who witnesses the argument.

700
00:30:37,586 --> 00:30:39,588
Then you beg them not to kill you

701
00:30:39,671 --> 00:30:41,006
but they kill you anyway.

702
00:30:41,381 --> 00:30:43,342
So that's three lines.

703
00:30:44,593 --> 00:30:45,635
But it's an acting piece!

704
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:47,596
It's a two-day shoot!

705
00:30:47,971 --> 00:30:49,014
And an acting piece.

706
00:30:49,389 --> 00:30:50,766
[Gab] It's a tiny part,
but it's a start.

707
00:30:50,849 --> 00:30:52,517
Don't worry about this one.

708
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:54,770
Everyone starts with a small role.

709
00:30:56,271 --> 00:30:58,440
[Chin] At least it's an acting piece!

710
00:30:58,523 --> 00:30:59,733
[Gab] Just keep auditioning.

711
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:00,942
You'll get a big role eventually.

712
00:31:01,026 --> 00:31:02,736
I'm going to be in a movie!

713
00:31:03,195 --> 00:31:05,072
[shrieks]

714
00:31:07,199 --> 00:31:09,993
- [Noemi] What's happening?
- I got the part!

715
00:31:10,077 --> 00:31:11,620
[shrieks]

716
00:31:11,703 --> 00:31:13,497
I got the part!

717
00:31:15,207 --> 00:31:17,542
[cheerful music]

718
00:31:17,626 --> 00:31:20,003
Careful!

719
00:31:20,796 --> 00:31:23,340
- Aren't you tired?
- You're sweaty.

720
00:31:23,423 --> 00:31:24,841
It's all crooked.

721
00:31:24,925 --> 00:31:26,426
- [gasps]
- [Lora] Are you enjoying?

722
00:31:26,510 --> 00:31:28,011
- [Joey] Yes, Mom.
- [kid] Come on, Joey!

723
00:31:32,349 --> 00:31:33,975
- Hi.
- Hi.

724
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:36,395
- [Monsour] What's up?
- [Daisy] Sir Monsour!

725
00:31:36,478 --> 00:31:37,687
- [Kiray] Uncle Gab!
- Is that Kiray?

726
00:31:37,771 --> 00:31:39,773
- Kiray!
- [Lora] You're so pretty!

727
00:31:40,273 --> 00:31:42,067
[squeals]

728
00:31:42,150 --> 00:31:43,944
I didn't recognize you!

729
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:45,612
Everyone is having so much fun.

730
00:31:45,695 --> 00:31:47,364
Oh, yeah! I'm having fun.

731
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:49,408
- And the food...
- You like it?

732
00:31:49,491 --> 00:31:51,243
- It's okay?
- Of course!

733
00:31:51,785 --> 00:31:53,370
You saved some for us, right?

734
00:31:53,829 --> 00:31:55,330
Extra special for you, of course.

735
00:31:55,414 --> 00:31:56,415
I love it!

736
00:31:56,498 --> 00:31:57,666
[Matthew] Andrea?

737
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:00,127
[all cheering]

738
00:32:00,210 --> 00:32:01,461
- Whoa!
- [guest] Can I take one more?

739
00:32:01,545 --> 00:32:02,629
[Monsour] Of course.

740
00:32:02,712 --> 00:32:03,713
Oh, who's that?

741
00:32:03,797 --> 00:32:05,799
- [all cheering]
- [Andrea laughing]

742
00:32:07,759 --> 00:32:08,885
[Andrea] Love it!

743
00:32:08,969 --> 00:32:11,138
[crowd in unison] Sir Matthew!

744
00:32:11,221 --> 00:32:13,723
- [pops]
- [kids cheering]

745
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:26,570
- [kid] Which superhero are you?
- [Andrea] Oh!

746
00:32:26,862 --> 00:32:29,114
[Lav] Director. Indie Director.

747
00:32:29,197 --> 00:32:30,407
[Andrea] Hi, Mr. Lav!

748
00:32:31,491 --> 00:32:32,534
You made it!

749
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:33,994
Is it over? Can I go home now?

750
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:36,163
Come on, you just got here.
You can't leave.

751
00:32:36,246 --> 00:32:37,747
We just wrapped the children's party.

752
00:32:37,831 --> 00:32:39,833
It's the adults' turn this time.

753
00:32:39,916 --> 00:32:41,918
Our receptionist Sofie here...

754
00:32:42,002 --> 00:32:43,545
- Hi!
- ...auditioned for a movie

755
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:45,672
and she got the role!
We're celebrating her!

756
00:32:45,755 --> 00:32:48,049
- Congratulations!
- [Sofie] Thank you so much, sir!

757
00:32:48,133 --> 00:32:50,260
And someone wants to speak to you.

758
00:32:50,343 --> 00:32:52,220
Oh, here we go. I knew it.

759
00:32:52,554 --> 00:32:53,597
Come on, do it.

760
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:55,390
This talk will fix everything.

761
00:32:55,474 --> 00:32:57,184
- Mon? Hi!
- Yeah?

762
00:32:57,267 --> 00:32:58,351
- Hi!
- Surprise!

763
00:32:58,810 --> 00:33:00,061
- Very surprising.
- All good, right?

764
00:33:00,145 --> 00:33:01,229
Sure.

765
00:33:01,313 --> 00:33:02,314
Indeed, it is.

766
00:33:02,397 --> 00:33:03,398
- Mm-hm.
- Surprise.

767
00:33:03,732 --> 00:33:04,774
Well...

768
00:33:04,858 --> 00:33:06,026
What can I get you, sir?

769
00:33:06,109 --> 00:33:07,319
The strongest drink you have.

770
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,737
You heard him.

771
00:33:11,698 --> 00:33:12,866
Thank you.

772
00:33:15,952 --> 00:33:17,329
- Sir.
- Uh... Mm-hm.

773
00:33:17,412 --> 00:33:18,788
So...

774
00:33:19,372 --> 00:33:22,375
I think it's time to finally talk
about your project...

775
00:33:22,459 --> 00:33:24,586
Here? At a children's party?

776
00:33:24,836 --> 00:33:27,255
Oh, we can go to the conference room

777
00:33:27,339 --> 00:33:30,133
where it's more private, more adult,
and hopefully more civilized.

778
00:33:30,425 --> 00:33:32,177
- Right? Let's go. Follow me!
- Okay.

779
00:33:32,260 --> 00:33:33,303
Sure.

780
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:38,099
[Lora] Rina!

781
00:33:38,183 --> 00:33:40,018
- The food was so good!
- It was!

782
00:33:40,101 --> 00:33:42,771
- Thank you!
- Anything for these guys.

783
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:43,855
Thank you!

784
00:33:43,939 --> 00:33:45,440
- Excuse me.
- Okay.

785
00:33:45,524 --> 00:33:46,525
Uh...

786
00:33:47,108 --> 00:33:48,318
I'm going to stay for a bit.

787
00:33:48,610 --> 00:33:49,694
I'll just visit you guys later.

788
00:33:49,778 --> 00:33:53,198
You don't have to. Look at this guy.
He's already tired.

789
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:56,493
Oh, there's no more playing tonight.

790
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:57,994
We'll see you at the airport, right?

791
00:33:58,078 --> 00:33:59,871
- I will.
- Then stay here

792
00:33:59,955 --> 00:34:01,289
and play with them.

793
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:03,083
Don't take us home. I'll handle it.

794
00:34:03,166 --> 00:34:04,668
- Are you sure? Okay.
- Yes.

795
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:06,586
Thank you.

796
00:34:07,212 --> 00:34:09,339
[indistinct chatter]

797
00:34:09,422 --> 00:34:12,259
[Noemi] You've drunk way too much.

798
00:34:12,926 --> 00:34:13,969
[loud crash]

799
00:34:14,052 --> 00:34:15,887
[indistinct shouting]

800
00:34:15,971 --> 00:34:17,013
[Gab] What was that?

801
00:34:19,474 --> 00:34:21,101
- You're walking out on me?
- Stop this!

802
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:22,519
- You're angry at me?
- Please!

803
00:34:22,602 --> 00:34:23,770
- Talk it out!
- Show me that anger!

804
00:34:23,853 --> 00:34:26,064
I'm not angry!
When I'm angry, I make a movie!

805
00:34:26,147 --> 00:34:27,440
- You're the one who's angry!
- Oh, my.

806
00:34:27,524 --> 00:34:29,526
- [Andrea] Please stop!
- I don't understand your anger!

807
00:34:29,609 --> 00:34:31,820
- [Lav jeers]
- Show it to me!

808
00:34:31,903 --> 00:34:33,613
I'll show you!

809
00:34:33,905 --> 00:34:35,574
- That's one!
- [all shout]

810
00:34:35,657 --> 00:34:36,783
Two!

811
00:34:36,866 --> 00:34:38,201
[indistinct shouting]

812
00:34:38,285 --> 00:34:40,620
Mon! Stop! Please!

813
00:34:41,705 --> 00:34:43,164
Three!

814
00:34:43,248 --> 00:34:44,499
And my finishing move!

815
00:34:44,583 --> 00:34:46,042
[shouts]

816
00:34:46,126 --> 00:34:47,794
- Well, what the heck!
- Come on!

817
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:50,589
- Now I'm getting serious!
- Come on!

818
00:34:50,672 --> 00:34:52,757
- Let's see what you got!
- Come on!

819
00:34:53,049 --> 00:34:54,718
[Andrea] Mother!

820
00:34:54,801 --> 00:34:55,802
- [Monsour] Mother!
- Hey!

821
00:34:55,885 --> 00:34:57,262
- Good evening, Mother!
- Mother Aleta.

822
00:34:57,345 --> 00:34:58,513
- Good evening.
- What's this about?

823
00:34:58,597 --> 00:34:59,889
Good evening, Mother.

824
00:34:59,973 --> 00:35:01,224
[Monsour] Good evening, Mother Aleta.

825
00:35:01,683 --> 00:35:02,851
This is just a rehearsal, ma'am.

826
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:05,020
- We're just fooling around.
- [Lav] This is just practice.

827
00:35:05,478 --> 00:35:08,189
- [Monsour] Just practicing.
- [Lav] Idiot.

828
00:35:08,565 --> 00:35:10,233
You were supposed to talk it out

829
00:35:10,317 --> 00:35:12,277
with your mouths, not your fists!

830
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:13,862
You boys drive me crazy!

831
00:35:14,529 --> 00:35:15,697
This is your fault, man!

832
00:35:16,114 --> 00:35:18,825
- You started it!
- You pulled my hair!

833
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:20,327
I did not pull your hair!

834
00:35:20,410 --> 00:35:22,287
- I just tugged at it.
- [Andrea shouts]

835
00:35:22,370 --> 00:35:23,663
My god!

836
00:35:23,747 --> 00:35:25,373
Will you listen to yourselves?

837
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:28,084
It's like talking to schoolkids here!

838
00:35:28,835 --> 00:35:31,004
Now will you please start over?

839
00:35:32,589 --> 00:35:33,840
- Hey, buddy.
- Hm?

840
00:35:35,050 --> 00:35:36,468
So that's the way you look at things?

841
00:35:36,551 --> 00:35:38,887
I mean, your eyesight, your vision?
That's the only way you see things?

842
00:35:38,970 --> 00:35:40,930
I'm not completely color blind.

843
00:35:41,014 --> 00:35:42,724
I see blues and greens.

844
00:35:42,932 --> 00:35:44,517
- Just like dogs.
- No red?

845
00:35:44,601 --> 00:35:45,894
- No red.
- Well, we need that.

846
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:47,103
Let me tell you this.

847
00:35:47,395 --> 00:35:49,522
The action movies you used to make?

848
00:35:49,606 --> 00:35:51,858
Those with "ratatatat",
you against a hundred men?

849
00:35:51,941 --> 00:35:53,151
[Lav] Pow, pow, pow!

850
00:35:53,234 --> 00:35:54,903
That's all gone. It's different now.

851
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:56,404
[Monsour]
But that's what I'm used to.

852
00:35:56,488 --> 00:35:59,824
How can I make
a comeback movie, when...

853
00:36:00,909 --> 00:36:03,036
I can't do drama?

854
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:04,537
Yeah, right, you can't.

855
00:36:06,039 --> 00:36:07,207
But you know

856
00:36:07,290 --> 00:36:09,125
- I did read your script.
- [Lav] And?

857
00:36:09,209 --> 00:36:10,627
- [Monsour] I loved it.
- [Lav] But?

858
00:36:10,710 --> 00:36:13,713
But it doesn't go with my brand.

859
00:36:13,797 --> 00:36:15,757
- It's too...
- Authentic.

860
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:17,425
- [finger snaps]
- That's it! It's too real.

861
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:20,887
You see, I make movies

862
00:36:21,179 --> 00:36:23,515
so that people can escape reality.

863
00:36:23,598 --> 00:36:25,016
And I make films to reveal the truth.

864
00:36:25,809 --> 00:36:27,227
[Rina] How are your superpowers
holding up?

865
00:36:28,770 --> 00:36:30,188
I have to look after these guys.

866
00:36:30,271 --> 00:36:32,107
They might kill each other again.

867
00:36:32,982 --> 00:36:33,983
Relax.

868
00:36:34,067 --> 00:36:36,736
- Will you sit?
- But!

869
00:36:36,820 --> 00:36:38,530
- Don't fly off in that cape!
- They drive me nuts!

870
00:36:39,239 --> 00:36:40,865
You should have used your power!

871
00:36:40,949 --> 00:36:42,951
[Andrea] It's one for all,
all for one!

872
00:36:43,368 --> 00:36:46,287
- I was really feeling my outfit!
- [laughs]

873
00:36:46,371 --> 00:36:47,956
It looks good on you!

874
00:36:48,039 --> 00:36:51,126
Speaking of which,
do you have extra clothes for later?

875
00:36:52,335 --> 00:36:55,588
If you go to work wearing that

876
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:57,507
you're going to get strange looks!

877
00:36:57,966 --> 00:36:59,551
I remembered.

878
00:37:01,469 --> 00:37:02,721
[giggles]

879
00:37:04,848 --> 00:37:06,182
[in English] What if...

880
00:37:06,266 --> 00:37:07,267
What?

881
00:37:09,936 --> 00:37:11,396
What if I move in with you?

882
00:37:12,105 --> 00:37:14,107
[playful music]

883
00:37:16,443 --> 00:37:17,485
Wow.

884
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:22,282
[Noemi] My god!

885
00:37:22,365 --> 00:37:26,369
Of all the places to fight in,
they choose the fountain!

886
00:37:26,453 --> 00:37:27,746
[Camille] Hey, Noemi!

887
00:37:27,829 --> 00:37:31,124
Hey, let me get that!

888
00:37:31,207 --> 00:37:33,376
You can go back inside.
Don't you want to party with them?

889
00:37:33,460 --> 00:37:35,587
Why are you always after what's mine?

890
00:37:36,087 --> 00:37:37,714
Aren't you satisfied yet?

891
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:49,517
Are you okay? Is this a bad time?

892
00:37:49,601 --> 00:37:51,519
What is it, Ms. Karylle?

893
00:37:51,603 --> 00:37:53,688
I'm working on a little project.

894
00:37:53,772 --> 00:37:55,190
Do you have time to help me?

895
00:37:55,565 --> 00:37:57,609
What's it about?

896
00:37:57,692 --> 00:37:59,736
It's the socials
for my Diva In Disguise persona.

897
00:38:00,945 --> 00:38:05,283
Oh, I can try,
but I'm no good with stuff like that.

898
00:38:05,366 --> 00:38:09,454
Besides, your mom
might not like this.

899
00:38:09,788 --> 00:38:12,332
She won't be involved in this.
It's just the two of us.

900
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:14,876
And maybe Chin would like to join us.

901
00:38:15,877 --> 00:38:16,920
Um...

902
00:38:17,003 --> 00:38:18,922
I don't think he'll want to help me.

903
00:38:19,923 --> 00:38:21,341
I don't think they like me very much.

904
00:38:23,510 --> 00:38:26,012
It's fine, don't stress over it.

905
00:38:27,055 --> 00:38:28,056
[chuckles]

906
00:38:28,598 --> 00:38:29,599
[tuts]

907
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:32,727
[giggles] This will be
our own little thing, okay?

908
00:38:32,977 --> 00:38:34,270
- [Karylle] Okay?
- Sure, I'll help you.

909
00:38:34,354 --> 00:38:35,355
[giggles]

910
00:38:41,361 --> 00:38:43,363
[approaching footsteps]

911
00:38:48,743 --> 00:38:49,744
[sighs]

912
00:38:52,747 --> 00:38:53,748
[exhales sharply]

913
00:38:58,503 --> 00:38:59,629
So how are you?

914
00:39:02,507 --> 00:39:03,633
[in English] Not too good.

915
00:39:08,721 --> 00:39:10,098
What would Samuel do?

916
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:15,645
[in Filipino] You taught me that.

917
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:22,110
But not everything
that Samuel did was right.

918
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:24,737
Matthew.

919
00:39:25,697 --> 00:39:26,906
Put in the work.

920
00:39:28,116 --> 00:39:29,534
You do the thinking.

921
00:39:29,617 --> 00:39:31,244
You figure out what you need to do.

922
00:39:31,995 --> 00:39:33,496
Samuel is dead.

923
00:39:34,747 --> 00:39:36,249
Stop bothering him.

924
00:39:38,751 --> 00:39:39,752
Okay.

925
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:41,212
Time for me to go.

926
00:39:41,421 --> 00:39:43,172
You just got here
and you're going home already?

927
00:39:45,008 --> 00:39:46,009
And you?

928
00:39:46,926 --> 00:39:48,261
Do you still go home?

929
00:39:55,852 --> 00:39:57,437
[frustrated sigh]

930
00:39:58,563 --> 00:40:00,023
Call my driver, I'm leaving.

931
00:40:05,612 --> 00:40:06,654
Hey!

932
00:40:06,863 --> 00:40:07,906
[Sofie] Hey, Sir Gab!

933
00:40:07,989 --> 00:40:08,990
What are you doing here?

934
00:40:09,657 --> 00:40:11,159
Trying to sober up.

935
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:12,744
I couldn't keep up with the others!

936
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:18,708
Thank you.

937
00:40:19,709 --> 00:40:20,710
For what?

938
00:40:22,378 --> 00:40:24,923
For Joey. He was so happy!

939
00:40:25,506 --> 00:40:26,633
Did you see him?

940
00:40:27,008 --> 00:40:28,259
That huge smile never left his face.

941
00:40:28,343 --> 00:40:30,178
I think it only disappeared
when he fell asleep.

942
00:40:31,721 --> 00:40:34,682
Come on, Sir Gab.
I'd do anything for Joey.

943
00:40:39,729 --> 00:40:40,813
And for you too.

944
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:42,106
Sir Gab.

945
00:40:44,609 --> 00:40:46,069
Thank you so much

946
00:40:46,444 --> 00:40:48,071
for believing in me.

947
00:40:48,988 --> 00:40:50,615
Thank you very much.

948
00:40:51,866 --> 00:40:54,911
I mean, look at me.
I'm going to be in a movie!

949
00:40:55,787 --> 00:40:57,747
I still can't believe it.

950
00:40:58,414 --> 00:41:00,291
Well, you deserve it.

951
00:41:01,834 --> 00:41:04,545
Hey! Monsour and Lav are at it again!

952
00:41:04,796 --> 00:41:06,005
[Gab] Hey, what's going on?

953
00:41:06,089 --> 00:41:07,632
[staff] It's Mr. Lav and Sir Monsour!

954
00:41:08,508 --> 00:41:10,677
- [Sofie] Huh?
- [Gab] Mr. Lav.

955
00:41:10,760 --> 00:41:12,887
- Bang! Bang!
- [Lav laughs]

956
00:41:12,971 --> 00:41:14,806
A quick step backward and bam!

957
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:15,890
Oh, gosh.

958
00:41:15,974 --> 00:41:17,934
Then I turn to them and go...
[imitates gun fires]

959
00:41:18,017 --> 00:41:21,646
I'll go after the master and go

960
00:41:21,729 --> 00:41:23,564
"Bam! Take that!"

961
00:41:23,648 --> 00:41:25,316
Huge explosion, man!

962
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:26,859
That's how we made movies back then!

963
00:41:26,943 --> 00:41:27,944
[Lav] I saw that, man!

964
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:29,028
And your movie Fierce!

965
00:41:29,112 --> 00:41:30,279
It's so wild, man!

966
00:41:30,363 --> 00:41:31,364
Heck, no!

967
00:41:31,447 --> 00:41:32,991
- So freaking wild!
- Wild?

968
00:41:33,074 --> 00:41:34,158
What about you?

969
00:41:34,242 --> 00:41:37,954
You made a head
with another face at the back!

970
00:41:38,746 --> 00:41:41,207
And that thing
you had Charo Santos do?

971
00:41:41,499 --> 00:41:45,086
Looking for her son on the floor
while the camera spun around her?

972
00:41:45,169 --> 00:41:48,381
Man, if that isn't crazy! Wild!

973
00:41:48,464 --> 00:41:51,384
Not everyone
who's at the top is successful.

974
00:41:52,260 --> 00:41:54,929
And not everyone at the bottom
is a loser.

975
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:57,348
We each have a place in this world.

976
00:41:58,141 --> 00:42:02,061
Wherever you are right now,
you're there

977
00:42:02,562 --> 00:42:05,356
because you are the only one
who can do what you do.

978
00:42:06,107 --> 00:42:07,692
That should be your attitude.

979
00:42:15,366 --> 00:42:18,703
[rock music]

980
00:42:43,728 --> 00:42:45,730
[man snores]

981
00:42:48,733 --> 00:42:50,735
[snoring continues]

982
00:42:52,487 --> 00:42:53,654
We've been infiltrated.

983
00:43:01,996 --> 00:43:03,331
- Did you see it?
- What happened?

984
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:05,583
- You saw it?
- How did Ogie know?

985
00:43:05,666 --> 00:43:06,667
I have no idea.

986
00:43:06,751 --> 00:43:07,752
Where's Matthew?

987
00:43:07,835 --> 00:43:09,003
I've been texting him.

988
00:43:09,087 --> 00:43:10,171
How did the press find out...

989
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:11,297
Deo?

990
00:43:11,547 --> 00:43:13,174
The AC's still not working!

991
00:43:13,257 --> 00:43:15,051
What happened? Have you fixed it?

992
00:43:15,927 --> 00:43:16,928
Someone broke in.

993
00:43:17,011 --> 00:43:18,429
- Someone broke in?
- Into the AC?

994
00:43:18,638 --> 00:43:19,847
[Chin] Oh, it's so cheap.

995
00:43:20,181 --> 00:43:21,808
- [Camille shushes]
- Hey.

996
00:43:21,891 --> 00:43:23,893
[shushes]

997
00:43:23,976 --> 00:43:25,394
[whispers] There's someone in there!

998
00:43:25,478 --> 00:43:26,938
[Sofie] What? Someone broke in?

999
00:43:27,480 --> 00:43:28,481
Who is it?

1000
00:43:28,564 --> 00:43:29,565
What do we do?

1001
00:43:29,649 --> 00:43:31,818
- Let's make our move.
- Go ahead.

1002
00:43:31,901 --> 00:43:33,277
Someone call security.

1003
00:43:33,361 --> 00:43:34,570
Wait!

1004
00:43:34,654 --> 00:43:36,739
No, wait. You have the key, right?

1005
00:43:37,281 --> 00:43:38,282
So use it!

1006
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:40,326
[indistinct chatter]

1007
00:43:40,409 --> 00:43:41,452
[Chin] Hey!

1008
00:43:41,536 --> 00:43:42,537
[Gab] Be careful!

1009
00:43:42,912 --> 00:43:45,498
[Daisy] How did he get inside?

1010
00:43:45,581 --> 00:43:47,041
[Camille] It's Sir Matthew's office!

1011
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:49,127
[Daisy] Who could that be?

1012
00:43:50,753 --> 00:43:52,130
- [gasps]
- [Gab] Sorry!

1013
00:43:52,213 --> 00:43:53,589
[Daisy] You pushed her!

1014
00:43:57,093 --> 00:43:58,469
- [Gab] Hey!
- [Camille] Deo, no!

1015
00:43:59,387 --> 00:44:00,888
You're a janitor, not a murderer!

1016
00:44:02,014 --> 00:44:03,015
- [thuds]
- [Matthew yells]

1017
00:44:03,099 --> 00:44:04,725
What?

1018
00:44:05,977 --> 00:44:06,978
[grunts]

1019
00:44:07,270 --> 00:44:08,271
[Andrea] Matthew?

1020
00:44:08,354 --> 00:44:09,438
- [Gab] Matty?
- [Noemi] Sir Matt?

1021
00:44:09,522 --> 00:44:11,232
- [Chin] Did they say it was Matthew?
- [Gab] How...

1022
00:44:11,315 --> 00:44:12,441
Two weeks?

1023
00:44:13,693 --> 00:44:14,819
Something like that.

1024
00:44:15,403 --> 00:44:16,404
Wait.

1025
00:44:16,863 --> 00:44:18,698
So you knew Camille was his daughter?

1026
00:44:19,198 --> 00:44:22,034
My god, of course not!
If I knew, then you would too.

1027
00:44:22,118 --> 00:44:23,119
Maybe you kept it from me.

1028
00:44:23,202 --> 00:44:25,246
Why didn't you tell us?

1029
00:44:25,872 --> 00:44:27,874
[hesitates] Maybe I was embarrassed.

1030
00:44:28,541 --> 00:44:30,459
- What's happening?
- I don't know.

1031
00:44:30,543 --> 00:44:31,669
- Wait.
- It's so hot.

1032
00:44:32,378 --> 00:44:33,921
You're ashamed that she's your kid?

1033
00:44:34,005 --> 00:44:35,006
No!

1034
00:44:35,089 --> 00:44:36,674
I'm ashamed to admit it to you guys.

1035
00:44:37,675 --> 00:44:39,218
- Matthew.
- Well...

1036
00:44:39,760 --> 00:44:41,095
I didn't want to impose.

1037
00:44:41,846 --> 00:44:44,140
I didn't wanna ask you to hide this

1038
00:44:45,016 --> 00:44:46,058
and lie to everyone else.

1039
00:44:46,142 --> 00:44:47,226
Come on, Matty.

1040
00:44:47,685 --> 00:44:48,686
You didn't have to hide.

1041
00:44:48,769 --> 00:44:51,272
And why stay here at the office?

1042
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:53,191
You could've stayed at a hotel.

1043
00:44:53,482 --> 00:44:56,027
Don't tell me money is an issue.

1044
00:44:56,903 --> 00:44:58,779
Aah!

1045
00:44:58,863 --> 00:44:59,864
What?

1046
00:45:00,990 --> 00:45:02,200
Oh, my god.

1047
00:45:04,410 --> 00:45:05,453
You don't have to do that.

1048
00:45:07,121 --> 00:45:08,331
I'll tell you everything.

1049
00:45:10,666 --> 00:45:11,667
That surprised me.

1050
00:45:11,751 --> 00:45:12,793
We already know.

1051
00:45:13,628 --> 00:45:14,629
Noemi, go ahead.

1052
00:45:18,466 --> 00:45:20,801
There's something between
you and Sir Matthew.

1053
00:45:21,093 --> 00:45:23,095
[whimpers]

1054
00:45:25,223 --> 00:45:26,682
Matthew's my father.

1055
00:45:34,065 --> 00:45:35,233
Hec is your brother?

1056
00:45:39,487 --> 00:45:41,030
Did you come to Manila

1057
00:45:41,113 --> 00:45:44,242
to ask Matthew to help you get work?

1058
00:45:44,992 --> 00:45:45,993
No.

1059
00:45:47,662 --> 00:45:49,163
I don't know, maybe.

1060
00:45:51,207 --> 00:45:52,541
[Camille] All I know is...

1061
00:45:53,542 --> 00:45:55,211
I want to be with him.

1062
00:45:58,130 --> 00:46:00,091
I want to get to know him again.

1063
00:46:01,133 --> 00:46:02,176
Wow, Noemi.

1064
00:46:02,927 --> 00:46:04,637
Looks like this fight is unfair.

1065
00:46:05,429 --> 00:46:06,847
We have to be really extra now.

1066
00:46:06,931 --> 00:46:09,225
[Sofie] The bosses aren't like that.

1067
00:46:09,308 --> 00:46:10,309
How do you know?

1068
00:46:11,477 --> 00:46:12,478
[scoffs]

1069
00:46:12,561 --> 00:46:16,857
Yeah, we're not sure
who to trust here.

1070
00:46:17,316 --> 00:46:18,526
I should go.

1071
00:46:18,901 --> 00:46:20,569
I need to give out calling cards.

1072
00:46:20,653 --> 00:46:23,155
I'm interested in becoming
a Junior Manager, Chin.

1073
00:46:23,239 --> 00:46:24,240
Really?

1074
00:46:25,199 --> 00:46:28,953
Why should we believe
anything you say?

1075
00:46:30,121 --> 00:46:31,122
Come on, Noemi.

1076
00:46:33,541 --> 00:46:34,959
[Daisy] What are you guys doing here?

1077
00:46:39,297 --> 00:46:41,465
Let's go back to reception.

1078
00:46:43,342 --> 00:46:45,052
Don't worry about them.

1079
00:46:45,136 --> 00:46:47,930
They're just being mean
because they're so stressed out.

1080
00:46:48,014 --> 00:46:49,348
- Come on!
- You go ahead.

1081
00:46:49,432 --> 00:46:50,474
I'll be there in a bit.

1082
00:46:50,850 --> 00:46:52,268
[Sofie] Okay,
don't make me wait too long.

1083
00:47:00,818 --> 00:47:02,403
What are we going to do, Matt?

1084
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:05,740
We already told everyone
we're buying SAM.

1085
00:47:06,032 --> 00:47:08,951
And this thing with Brandon,
how did this get out?

1086
00:47:09,035 --> 00:47:10,911
The advertisers will kill us!

1087
00:47:11,412 --> 00:47:13,789
It's been out since last night.
I even saw it.

1088
00:47:14,498 --> 00:47:15,750
But it was too late to do anything.

1089
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:17,960
[in English] But don't worry,
I'll take care of that.

1090
00:47:18,544 --> 00:47:19,587
And SAM?

1091
00:47:20,463 --> 00:47:21,505
I'll handle that too.

1092
00:47:21,922 --> 00:47:23,090
You just have to...

1093
00:47:23,716 --> 00:47:24,842
You just have to trust me.

1094
00:47:26,177 --> 00:47:28,137
Okay, but, Matt...

1095
00:47:28,929 --> 00:47:30,806
You can't stay here anymore.

1096
00:47:31,766 --> 00:47:33,642
[in Filipino]
Don't do this to yourself!

1097
00:47:35,144 --> 00:47:39,315
I'd let you stay with me,
but Rina's moving in.

1098
00:47:39,857 --> 00:47:41,192
Oh, wow, congrats!

1099
00:47:41,275 --> 00:47:42,860
- I know, right?
- Oh, wow indeed.

1100
00:47:42,943 --> 00:47:43,944
Congratulations!

1101
00:47:44,028 --> 00:47:45,196
Thank you!

1102
00:47:47,073 --> 00:47:48,074
Fine.

1103
00:47:48,157 --> 00:47:49,241
You can stay with me.

1104
00:47:50,117 --> 00:47:51,827
[in English]
Just until we figure everything out.

1105
00:47:52,328 --> 00:47:54,080
- You sure?
- I'm sure.

1106
00:47:54,163 --> 00:47:55,247
[in Filipino] Go shower.

1107
00:47:55,581 --> 00:47:56,832
We have a lot of work to do.

1108
00:47:57,375 --> 00:47:58,376
Thank you.

1109
00:48:01,128 --> 00:48:03,756
[thrilling music]

1110
00:48:08,761 --> 00:48:11,597
[inaudible dialogue]

1111
00:48:11,680 --> 00:48:13,474
Why is it so hot here?

1112
00:48:13,557 --> 00:48:16,602
- Gross, you haven't paid your bill?
- Oh, sorry.

1113
00:48:16,685 --> 00:48:18,229
- Megan? Hi!
- Hi!

1114
00:48:18,312 --> 00:48:19,772
I missed you!

1115
00:48:19,855 --> 00:48:21,857
- How are you?
- I'm okay!

1116
00:48:21,941 --> 00:48:25,152
- I missed you! Say hi to my vlog!
- Hi!

1117
00:48:27,947 --> 00:48:29,198
Hi, Sir Gab.

1118
00:48:29,281 --> 00:48:30,282
- [Yuki] Hello!
- Hey, Yuki!

1119
00:48:30,366 --> 00:48:31,700
- Hi!
- [Gab] Hi!

1120
00:48:31,784 --> 00:48:32,993
- How are you...
- It's hot.

1121
00:48:33,077 --> 00:48:35,079
Sorry, the AC is being fixed.

1122
00:48:35,162 --> 00:48:36,997
- Here, use this.
- [Yuki] Thank you.

1123
00:48:37,665 --> 00:48:38,666
How may I help you?

1124
00:48:39,125 --> 00:48:40,751
[sighs] Okay, here goes.

1125
00:48:40,835 --> 00:48:43,337
So I wanted to stay in this hotel
with my friends

1126
00:48:43,421 --> 00:48:45,047
we want to celebrate his birthday.

1127
00:48:45,131 --> 00:48:47,550
Because you know, 22 is huge, right?

1128
00:48:47,633 --> 00:48:49,176
I mean, 22 years on this Earth!

1129
00:48:49,260 --> 00:48:51,053
- I'm so proud of him!
- Wow. Yay.

1130
00:48:51,137 --> 00:48:52,847
But the hotel backed out!

1131
00:48:53,347 --> 00:48:54,390
[Yuki] Like, they backed out.

1132
00:48:54,765 --> 00:48:56,809
- I'm super mad.
- [Gab] Wow, okay.

1133
00:48:56,892 --> 00:48:57,935
So sorry to hear that.

1134
00:48:58,018 --> 00:48:59,103
Did you get a refund?

1135
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:00,187
How much did you pay them?

1136
00:49:00,271 --> 00:49:02,356
- No, I wrote to them.
- You wrote them a check?

1137
00:49:02,773 --> 00:49:03,858
No, I emailed them.

1138
00:49:06,026 --> 00:49:08,237
- Huh?
- No, it's like this.

1139
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:10,030
[Yuki] I emailed them,
you know, the stuff.

1140
00:49:10,114 --> 00:49:12,825
I told them I wanna stay there
with my friends

1141
00:49:13,242 --> 00:49:15,411
and celebrate my friend's birthday.

1142
00:49:15,494 --> 00:49:18,372
You know, the works.

1143
00:49:18,456 --> 00:49:22,168
I told them
that I have 8.4 million followers...

1144
00:49:22,251 --> 00:49:23,377
Wait, let me check.

1145
00:49:23,461 --> 00:49:24,837
Yup, it's 8.4 million followers.

1146
00:49:24,920 --> 00:49:27,089
And we're going to promote them

1147
00:49:27,173 --> 00:49:28,799
on all my social media platforms.

1148
00:49:28,883 --> 00:49:30,217
And you know how it goes...

1149
00:49:30,301 --> 00:49:32,636
the shebang, shebang, the richness.

1150
00:49:32,720 --> 00:49:33,846
All that. But...

1151
00:49:38,851 --> 00:49:39,894
They backed out!

1152
00:49:41,353 --> 00:49:42,354
Man, it's hot.

1153
00:49:42,438 --> 00:49:46,025
Uh, Yuki, "back out" means
you had a prior arrangement

1154
00:49:46,108 --> 00:49:48,027
but one of the parties "backed out".

1155
00:49:49,278 --> 00:49:51,864
[Gab] Here, it doesn't sound like
you had an arrangement at all.

1156
00:49:51,947 --> 00:49:53,407
No, but it's rude!

1157
00:49:53,491 --> 00:49:54,783
Like, it's so rude.

1158
00:49:54,867 --> 00:49:57,369
I mean, do they not know

1159
00:49:57,620 --> 00:49:59,747
what I can do for their business?

1160
00:49:59,830 --> 00:50:01,582
- [Yuki] Am I right?
- [Gab] Okay.

1161
00:50:01,665 --> 00:50:03,459
- [Yuki] They should appreciate me.
- [Gab] What...

1162
00:50:05,544 --> 00:50:06,670
What do you want us to do?

1163
00:50:07,421 --> 00:50:08,797
Well, you're my manager.

1164
00:50:08,881 --> 00:50:10,090
You know what to do.

1165
00:50:10,508 --> 00:50:12,134
So make them say yes.

1166
00:50:12,551 --> 00:50:13,552
[scoffs]

1167
00:50:14,303 --> 00:50:16,388
That's not how it works.

1168
00:50:18,057 --> 00:50:19,099
How does it work?

1169
00:50:19,183 --> 00:50:21,727
Chin? Noemi? Camille?

1170
00:50:22,478 --> 00:50:23,479
[Yuki] How?

1171
00:50:23,687 --> 00:50:24,688
Can you guys tell me?

1172
00:50:25,981 --> 00:50:28,984
[Chin] So, Yuki,
here's what we can do...

1173
00:50:33,864 --> 00:50:35,074
[chuckles]

1174
00:50:35,533 --> 00:50:36,700
Be careful what you wish for.

1175
00:50:37,076 --> 00:50:38,369
So now it's just me.

1176
00:50:39,078 --> 00:50:40,246
It sure is.

1177
00:50:40,329 --> 00:50:42,498
Just send Camille over
when you're done.

1178
00:50:43,249 --> 00:50:44,875
- [Gab] No, I'll do it.
- Go back in there.

1179
00:50:44,959 --> 00:50:45,960
- [Gab] What do you need?
- No.

1180
00:50:46,043 --> 00:50:47,044
I'll do it for you.

1181
00:50:49,797 --> 00:50:52,633
How are Sir Monsour and Mr. Lav?

1182
00:50:53,884 --> 00:50:55,094
They're still talking.

1183
00:51:00,057 --> 00:51:01,850
- [Andrea] Camille, can I trust you?
- Ma'am?

1184
00:51:02,351 --> 00:51:04,770
[in English]
Knowing that Matthew is your dad

1185
00:51:05,521 --> 00:51:06,897
and you work for me

1186
00:51:07,856 --> 00:51:08,899
can I trust you?

1187
00:51:09,233 --> 00:51:10,693
[in Filipino]
Of course you can, Ms. Andrea.

1188
00:51:11,527 --> 00:51:12,653
You can trust me.

1189
00:51:15,114 --> 00:51:16,115
[in English] Thank you.

1190
00:51:34,675 --> 00:51:35,759
[Karylle exclaims]

1191
00:51:36,594 --> 00:51:37,595
[Camille] Now...

1192
00:51:38,679 --> 00:51:40,222
everyone is doubting me.

1193
00:51:40,806 --> 00:51:41,932
[Karylle] Even Andrea?

1194
00:51:42,474 --> 00:51:43,517
[exhales sharply]

1195
00:51:43,601 --> 00:51:45,227
Especially Ms. Andrea.

1196
00:51:47,021 --> 00:51:48,897
It's an initial reaction.

1197
00:51:48,981 --> 00:51:50,024
I mean...

1198
00:51:50,608 --> 00:51:51,650
they were surprised.

1199
00:51:51,734 --> 00:51:55,070
They were bombarded with all
this info about you and Matthew.

1200
00:51:56,572 --> 00:51:57,948
But it'll sort itself out.

1201
00:51:58,741 --> 00:51:59,742
Soon.

1202
00:52:02,077 --> 00:52:04,622
No family is perfect.

1203
00:52:10,127 --> 00:52:12,087
Everything is gonna be okay.

1204
00:52:12,171 --> 00:52:14,214
[thrilling music]

1205
00:52:15,341 --> 00:52:16,634
WHAT'S THE TEA?
WITH OGIE DIAZ

1206
00:52:16,717 --> 00:52:19,303
All right, the latest from the mill.

1207
00:52:19,386 --> 00:52:20,596
I'm getting the jitters

1208
00:52:20,679 --> 00:52:23,390
because we've been talking
about breakups

1209
00:52:23,474 --> 00:52:25,309
celeb couple problems, politics.

1210
00:52:25,392 --> 00:52:27,936
But this one is different.

1211
00:52:28,020 --> 00:52:29,521
Check this out.

1212
00:52:29,605 --> 00:52:32,024
A popular actor...

1213
00:52:32,524 --> 00:52:33,776
Wait, is he still popular?

1214
00:52:33,859 --> 00:52:35,277
[laughs]

1215
00:52:35,361 --> 00:52:38,822
And a director. They made a scene.
That's right.

1216
00:52:38,906 --> 00:52:42,534
[Ogie] The two were invited
to the baptism

1217
00:52:42,618 --> 00:52:44,828
of a talent manager's child.

1218
00:52:44,912 --> 00:52:47,081
And what happened?

1219
00:52:47,164 --> 00:52:49,875
It was rooted
in the disagreements they had

1220
00:52:49,958 --> 00:52:52,419
from the action film they're doing.

1221
00:52:52,503 --> 00:52:54,171
It's crazy.

1222
00:52:54,254 --> 00:52:57,508
So, at the baptism,
things got heated really quickly.

1223
00:52:57,591 --> 00:53:00,302
It was an all out fistfight!

1224
00:53:00,386 --> 00:53:02,513
Kung Fu here, Karate there.

1225
00:53:02,596 --> 00:53:03,806
Goodness!

1226
00:53:03,889 --> 00:53:06,809
Both of them were soaked
with holy water!

1227
00:53:06,892 --> 00:53:08,352
Did that cleanse them of their sins?

1228
00:53:08,435 --> 00:53:10,729
[laughs] Of course not.

1229
00:53:10,813 --> 00:53:13,357
Mr. Director and Mr. Actor

1230
00:53:13,440 --> 00:53:15,859
start confessing your sins!

1231
00:53:15,943 --> 00:53:18,946
What you're doing isn't right.

1232
00:53:19,029 --> 00:53:20,823
You're driving me nuts.

1233
00:53:21,198 --> 00:53:23,283
WHAT'S THE TEA?
WITH OGIE DIAZ

1234
00:53:26,203 --> 00:53:27,496
Sorry about the mess.

1235
00:53:29,623 --> 00:53:30,624
It's okay.

1236
00:53:33,460 --> 00:53:35,379
Andrea is...

1237
00:53:35,963 --> 00:53:38,006
lending us her extra mattress.

1238
00:53:38,966 --> 00:53:40,384
Are you okay on the couch for now?

1239
00:53:40,467 --> 00:53:42,428
Yeah. Don't worry about me.

1240
00:53:42,511 --> 00:53:43,512
Actually...

1241
00:53:44,972 --> 00:53:47,182
this is softer than the one
at the office.

1242
00:53:53,188 --> 00:53:54,189
[Gab] Here you go.

1243
00:53:54,481 --> 00:53:55,482
Thank you!

1244
00:53:55,566 --> 00:53:56,567
Uh...

1245
00:53:56,650 --> 00:53:57,651
Matty.

1246
00:53:58,444 --> 00:53:59,445
It'll work out.

1247
00:54:00,779 --> 00:54:01,989
We'll find a way.

1248
00:54:02,281 --> 00:54:04,366
Yeah, thanks.

1249
00:54:04,450 --> 00:54:05,534
Oh, by the way.

1250
00:54:06,201 --> 00:54:07,286
Do you snore?

1251
00:54:07,369 --> 00:54:08,662
No, not me.

1252
00:54:09,288 --> 00:54:10,998
Good, I'm a light sleeper.

1253
00:54:11,248 --> 00:54:13,459
I can't room with someone who snores.

1254
00:54:13,792 --> 00:54:14,793
I wake up easily.

1255
00:54:15,085 --> 00:54:16,712
- No problem.
- Okay.

1256
00:54:17,171 --> 00:54:18,172
[Gab] Good night!

1257
00:54:18,255 --> 00:54:19,298
Yeah, good night!

1258
00:54:20,924 --> 00:54:22,926
[light music]

1259
00:54:32,019 --> 00:54:33,645
[Gab snores]

1260
00:54:37,900 --> 00:54:39,902
[snores]

1261
00:54:44,990 --> 00:54:46,617
[snores loudly]

1262
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:49,203
[Lav] Bam!

1263
00:54:50,037 --> 00:54:52,039
Pow, pow! You make a turn!

1264
00:54:52,331 --> 00:54:54,333
You hit! Kick!

1265
00:54:54,792 --> 00:54:56,960
Elbow! Bam!

1266
00:54:57,044 --> 00:54:58,170
Bam!

1267
00:54:58,253 --> 00:55:00,380
Explosion, take cover, run!

1268
00:55:00,464 --> 00:55:02,007
Run!

1269
00:55:02,090 --> 00:55:03,091
You take a tumble.

1270
00:55:03,175 --> 00:55:04,468
There's more by the door.

1271
00:55:04,551 --> 00:55:05,928
Bam, bam! You take their gun.

1272
00:55:06,011 --> 00:55:07,095
Tak! Tak! Tak!

1273
00:55:07,179 --> 00:55:08,388
Ratatatatat!

1274
00:55:08,889 --> 00:55:09,890
Simple.

1275
00:55:09,973 --> 00:55:11,058
That's it.

1276
00:55:11,141 --> 00:55:12,184
Very simple.

1277
00:55:12,684 --> 00:55:13,977
Lav, I have a question.

1278
00:55:14,061 --> 00:55:15,187
Don't worry about the blood!

1279
00:55:15,270 --> 00:55:16,438
It'll be all bloody!

1280
00:55:16,730 --> 00:55:17,856
Real and CGI!

1281
00:55:17,940 --> 00:55:20,526
I want to know

1282
00:55:20,609 --> 00:55:23,195
my character's motivation.

1283
00:55:23,654 --> 00:55:25,364
What drives my character.

1284
00:55:25,447 --> 00:55:26,448
Your what?

1285
00:55:27,199 --> 00:55:29,493
What I want to know is

1286
00:55:30,452 --> 00:55:32,329
where my character is coming from.

1287
00:55:33,872 --> 00:55:36,583
I mean, must he beat up everyone?

1288
00:55:36,667 --> 00:55:37,835
[Lav] It's an action movie.

1289
00:55:38,418 --> 00:55:41,046
Why not talk to them calmly?

1290
00:55:41,922 --> 00:55:43,674
That sounds like a good idea.

1291
00:55:44,758 --> 00:55:45,759
[clicks tongue]

1292
00:55:49,888 --> 00:55:50,931
Camille.

1293
00:55:52,558 --> 00:55:54,017
- [Camille] Yes, sir?
- What's up with him?

1294
00:55:54,977 --> 00:55:56,019
He's going method on me.

1295
00:55:56,478 --> 00:55:57,479
This is an action movie.

1296
00:55:58,063 --> 00:55:59,064
I don't...

1297
00:55:59,147 --> 00:56:00,232
- [Lav] Talk to him.
- I don't...

1298
00:56:00,315 --> 00:56:01,692
I want the old him back.

1299
00:56:02,609 --> 00:56:04,152
How much longer, Deo?

1300
00:56:04,736 --> 00:56:06,071
The heat is unbearable!

1301
00:56:10,117 --> 00:56:11,660
I know what I must do.

1302
00:56:13,287 --> 00:56:14,580
But I'm only human.

1303
00:56:16,039 --> 00:56:17,958
And when the bough breaks

1304
00:56:18,667 --> 00:56:19,793
the cradle will fall.

1305
00:56:21,295 --> 00:56:23,338
You broke the bough, SAM!

1306
00:56:25,257 --> 00:56:26,341
[Sofie] What?

1307
00:56:27,593 --> 00:56:28,886
There is an end to everything.

1308
00:56:29,678 --> 00:56:30,804
Let me go get the vacuum cleaner.

1309
00:56:31,930 --> 00:56:32,931
It's so hot!

1310
00:56:33,015 --> 00:56:34,766
We're a devil short of hell here!

1311
00:56:35,434 --> 00:56:36,435
- Gab!
- Yeah?

1312
00:56:37,269 --> 00:56:38,270
Where's Matt?

1313
00:56:38,729 --> 00:56:40,022
He still won't get up.

1314
00:56:41,148 --> 00:56:42,941
He's got a lot of work to do.

1315
00:56:43,025 --> 00:56:44,693
Let's give him space.

1316
00:56:44,776 --> 00:56:45,903
He'll get up soon.

1317
00:56:46,737 --> 00:56:48,238
To vanquish us all?

1318
00:56:48,906 --> 00:56:50,240
[chuckles] He might.

1319
00:56:50,324 --> 00:56:51,575
[laughs]

1320
00:56:51,658 --> 00:56:52,659
I'm going.

1321
00:56:52,743 --> 00:56:53,744
Home?

1322
00:56:54,244 --> 00:56:55,412
I told you.

1323
00:56:55,495 --> 00:56:57,581
Rina's moving in today.

1324
00:56:57,664 --> 00:56:58,999
It will be a few trips back and forth

1325
00:56:59,082 --> 00:57:00,208
so I have to be home.

1326
00:57:00,292 --> 00:57:01,835
Well, you seem excited!

1327
00:57:01,919 --> 00:57:03,962
- [Gab] Okay. Take care!
- [Andrea] Bye! See you!

1328
00:57:05,088 --> 00:57:06,757
- Chin?
- Yes?

1329
00:57:06,840 --> 00:57:08,759
I need these photocopied, please.

1330
00:57:09,217 --> 00:57:11,595
- Four copies for our meeting later.
- Sure.

1331
00:57:11,678 --> 00:57:13,972
- I'll make it ten just to be sure.
- Okay, good.

1332
00:57:14,056 --> 00:57:15,223
START

1333
00:57:15,307 --> 00:57:18,852
[machine whirring]

1334
00:57:25,984 --> 00:57:27,319
- Will you be long?
- [Camille gasps]

1335
00:57:27,861 --> 00:57:28,862
[Camille] No. I'm done.

1336
00:57:32,074 --> 00:57:33,075
Almost done, sorry.

1337
00:57:34,910 --> 00:57:35,911
Just a few more.

1338
00:57:40,624 --> 00:57:41,625
Your turn.

1339
00:57:43,085 --> 00:57:45,170
- [Sofie] Thank you!
- Sof, I need your stapler.

1340
00:57:45,253 --> 00:57:46,254
[Sofie] Sure, here you go.

1341
00:57:46,630 --> 00:57:49,633
By the way,
Sir Gabriel also needs a copy.

1342
00:57:49,716 --> 00:57:51,134
- Sorry, I forgot.
- [Camille] Oh, okay.

1343
00:57:51,218 --> 00:57:52,219
It's fine.

1344
00:57:52,719 --> 00:57:53,762
I'll leave this here.

1345
00:57:55,263 --> 00:57:57,057
[Camille] Chin, are you done?

1346
00:57:57,140 --> 00:57:58,809
I need one more copy for...

1347
00:58:00,769 --> 00:58:02,437
You left this.

1348
00:58:02,521 --> 00:58:04,147
That might be important for your dad.

1349
00:58:08,777 --> 00:58:10,821
Please don't tell anyone.

1350
00:58:11,822 --> 00:58:12,823
He hasn't signed anything yet.

1351
00:58:12,906 --> 00:58:15,283
And he doesn't know I have a copy.

1352
00:58:15,742 --> 00:58:16,743
[Chin] Oh, please.

1353
00:58:16,910 --> 00:58:19,246
I don't care about any of that.
But I'm staying in SAM.

1354
00:58:19,955 --> 00:58:21,498
Should I tell Ms. Andrea?

1355
00:58:23,959 --> 00:58:24,960
You know what?

1356
00:58:25,585 --> 00:58:28,296
Stay out of it.
They'll just fight over this.

1357
00:58:28,380 --> 00:58:29,381
What happens to SAM?

1358
00:58:29,798 --> 00:58:31,425
I mean, can she and Sir Gab
handle SAM

1359
00:58:32,175 --> 00:58:33,510
without my dad...

1360
00:58:34,386 --> 00:58:35,512
without Sir Matthew?

1361
00:58:36,013 --> 00:58:37,305
That's not your problem.

1362
00:58:38,015 --> 00:58:39,224
Just stay out of it.

1363
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:44,521
Thank you, Chin.

1364
00:58:45,272 --> 00:58:46,606
Okay, sure.

1365
00:58:46,690 --> 00:58:48,692
[somber music]

1366
00:58:59,411 --> 00:59:01,329
[in English]
"Love me when I least deserve it."

1367
00:59:02,497 --> 00:59:03,623
[in Filipino] That's about right.

1368
00:59:04,458 --> 00:59:06,460
In your darkest moments

1369
00:59:07,461 --> 00:59:09,212
you'll need the power of true love.

1370
00:59:10,630 --> 00:59:12,507
I've asked this of so many women.

1371
00:59:13,967 --> 00:59:15,302
Only one agreed.

1372
00:59:23,226 --> 00:59:24,352
[Rina] Careful, babe.

1373
00:59:24,436 --> 00:59:25,729
[chuckles]

1374
00:59:25,812 --> 00:59:27,606
What is all this stuff, honey?

1375
00:59:28,523 --> 00:59:30,901
You said "move in",
so I'm moving in with everything.

1376
00:59:31,359 --> 00:59:33,820
- I think that's it for this batch.
- Okay.

1377
00:59:33,904 --> 00:59:36,114
How many more trips?

1378
00:59:36,198 --> 00:59:37,699
A couple more.

1379
00:59:38,158 --> 00:59:39,910
Okay.

1380
00:59:39,993 --> 00:59:41,328
- Go on now!
- Okay.

1381
00:59:41,661 --> 00:59:43,121
- I'll see you later!
- [Andrea] Yup!

1382
00:59:43,205 --> 00:59:44,206
Don't work too hard.

1383
00:59:44,289 --> 00:59:45,957
Hurry up, but be careful, okay?

1384
00:59:46,041 --> 00:59:47,876
- [Rina] Okay, bye, see you!
- Bye!

1385
00:59:49,878 --> 00:59:51,797
Okay.

1386
00:59:54,257 --> 00:59:56,843
[grunts]

1387
00:59:58,553 --> 01:00:00,847
You stand out, so you go first.

1388
01:00:01,556 --> 01:00:02,933
[clatters]

1389
01:00:04,142 --> 01:00:05,227
[gasps]

1390
01:00:07,270 --> 01:00:08,313
Okay.

1391
01:00:11,024 --> 01:00:12,275
[chuckles]

1392
01:00:54,442 --> 01:00:55,902
[exhales sharply]

1393
01:00:58,989 --> 01:01:01,575
[breathes heavily]

1394
01:01:03,493 --> 01:01:04,494
[frustrated yell]

1395
01:01:07,914 --> 01:01:09,916
[closing theme music]
